  "notes": "Composed of {速|そく} (fast/speed) and {読|どく} (reading). Refers to techniques for reading faster than normal while maintaining comprehension. Speed reading courses and books are popular in Japan, often marketed to students and businesspeople.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {速読|そくどく}{術|じゅつ}: speed reading technique\n- {速読|そくどく}{法|ほう}: speed reading method\n- {速読|そくどく}の{訓練|くんれん}: speed reading training\n- {速読|そくどく}する: to speed-read\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {多読|たどく}: extensive reading — reading a large volume of material, not necessarily fast\n- {精読|せいどく}: careful/close reading — reading slowly and thoroughly, the opposite approach\n- {音読|おんどく}: reading aloud — reading text out loud\n- {黙読|もくどく}: silent reading — reading without vocalizing",
